// The townsfolk's names and temperaments (GDD §3.1; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 453; docs/design/townsfolk.md). The numbers
// (the personality matrix, how names are drawn) are in tuning/townsfolk.json; this file is only words, read by
// Sim/Towns/TownFolk.
//
// How it's written (towns.json's rules hold): the voice is plain, dry, a little Maritime, never put on. A temperament's
// lines are how somebody carries the town's grief, not what the custom is: they never name a creature or its rule, so
// they sit in any town. Keep a line under ~150 characters, in the HUD's letters (ASCII and àâçéèêëîïôùûü). Placeholders:
// {town}, {law}, {hall}, {name}/{name2} (somebody else here), {other} (another town), {n} (a small number). Bynames:
// {first} is the given name; the surname follows the byname ("Holy Annie Gillis").
