  },

  // The temperaments (tuning/townsfolk.json "temperaments"): their bynames, and one line each person of them may say
  // (a deck: nobody in a town says another's).
  "temperaments": {
    "faithful": {
      "bynames": ["Holy {first}", "{first} Amen", "{first} the Deacon"],
      "lines": [
        "{law} I'd keep it twice if they let me.",
        "The council says once. I do it three times. Nobody I love has gone since I started.",
        "You're doing it wrong. Not wrong enough to die. Wrong enough to watch.",
        "I keep it for the ones who didn't. That's who it's for. Not you.",
        "They want to ease it. Ease it! Ask {hall} what easing it cost us the first winter.",
        "Every night I do it right, and every night I'm still here. That's not luck, b'y.",
        "{name} skips it some nights. I write it down. Somebody has to.",
        "When I die, keep it at my grave. Don't stop because I'm past needing it."
      ]
    },
    "doubter": {
      "bynames": ["{first} Maybe", "Doubting {first}", "{first} the Lawyer"],
      "lines": [
        "Half of it's grief and half of it's habit. Nobody can tell me which half saves you.",
        "I stopped keeping it for a month once. Nothing came. I started again anyway. Don't ask me why.",
        "It was one bad night, years back. We built a whole town on it.",
        "{other} does the opposite and they're still alive. Mostly.",
        "Don't tell the keeper I said so. I still do it. I only don't believe it.",
        "There's a reason in it somewhere. It's smaller than they make out.",
        "Nobody knows why it works. That's the honest answer, and you'll not hear it twice in {town}.",
        "Trust the first thing they tell you here. The rest grew on after, like moss."
      ]
    },
    "mourner": {
      "bynames": ["Black {first}", "{first} Waiting", "{first} Sorrow"],
      "lines": [
        "I talk to him at the window. Some nights the glass fogs on the other side.",
        "Nobody says her name now. I say it. Every morning. In case.",
        "You've the look of somebody I lost. Around the eyes. Don't mind me.",
        "I kept the coat. It still smells of the coal shed. That's all that's left that's his.",
        "Grief's a job here. Some of us work longer hours.",
        "If you see a woman out there in a blue scarf, don't stop. It isn't her. I know. I still look.",
        "They say it gets lighter. It doesn't. You only get stronger carrying it.",
        "Leave the door on the latch for them. ... No. Don't. I don't know why I said that."
      ]
    },
    "hollow": {
      "bynames": ["Quiet {first}", "{first} Grey", "Still {first}"],
      "lines": [
        "I don't feel the cold now. Or much else.",
        "We lost {n} that winter. I've stopped counting the ones since.",
        "You'll go out on the line and you'll come back or you won't. Either way the kettle's on at six.",
        "I used to be frightened. It took too long. I put it down.",
        "Ask somebody else. I've said all my words about it.",
        "Nothing changes in {town}. I like it that way. Nothing changing means nobody's gone.",
        "Every face in here I'll bury, or they'll bury me. I don't mind which.",
        "Funny. You stop hoping and you stop hurting about the same time."
      ]
    },
    "watcher": {
      "bynames": ["{first} Eyes", "{first} Count-Twice", "Hawk {first}"],
      "lines": [
        "From away, are you. Stand where I can see your hands.",
        "I watched you come in. I'll watch you go. I count both times.",
        "Say what you want and go on. We're not short of strangers who looked like friends.",
        "Don't take it personal. I look at everybody like this. My own mother. Her most of all.",
        "Last crew through said they'd write. Nobody's written.",
        "You keep looking at the wall. Why are you looking at the wall?",
        "I'll know you next time. I know everybody next time.",
        "Your boots are wet. It's not rained. Where've you been walking?"
      ]
    },
    "comforter": {
      "bynames": ["{first} Kettle", "Sweet {first}", "{first} Biscuit"],
      "lines": [
        "Sit a minute. There's tea. It's mostly tea.",
        "You've a long night ahead. Eat something. Go on. I made too much. I always make too much.",
        "I knit for the crews. Mitts, mostly. Somebody's always come back without them.",
        "We do what we can to make it a home. It's not much. It's something.",
        "Here. Take the heel of the loaf. It's lucky. Don't ask me who told me that.",
        "Come back and tell me how it went. Nobody ever comes back to tell me.",
        "You look like you've not slept. Nobody here has either. We're good company that way.",
        "There's a kitchen racket Saturdays. We keep it quiet. You'd be welcome."
      ]
    },
    "talker": {
      "bynames": ["{first} the Mouth", "Talking {first}", "{first} Telegraph"],
      "lines": [
        "{name} says it's on the roofs. {name2} says it's under the platform. I say it's both, and that's worse.",
        "You'll want to know about the line. I'll tell you what I heard, and you'll not like it.",
        "Don't listen to the keeper, listen to me. I listen to everybody.",
        "There was a crew through last spring that did it backwards. One came home. She told me all about it.",
        "I'm not supposed to say. So I'll say it quiet: it doesn't like what the law's about. That's why there's a law.",
        "{name} keeps a jar under the floor. Don't ask me what's in it. I'll tell you anyway. Teeth.",
        "Nobody has the whole story. I've got the most of it.",
        "The {hall} lot don't tell you the half. They tell you the half that makes them look good."
      ]
    },
    "frayed": {
      "bynames": ["Jumpy {first}", "Shaky {first}", "{first} Startle"],
      "lines": [
        "Did you hear that? ... No. No, you're right. Go on.",
        "I can't - sorry. I can't stand near the gate. Walk me back a ways?",
        "Don't come up on me from that side. Ever. I'll not be responsible.",
        "My hands shake. They've shaken since the second winter. I hold the cup with both.",
        "Every train that comes in, I think: that's the one. And it never is. And I think it again.",
        "Talk to me. Keep talking. When people stop talking is when I hear it.",
        "I sleep in my boots. You never know. You never know.",
        "Is it dark yet? I mean properly dark. Is it properly dark?"
      ]
    },
    "mender": {
      "bynames": ["{first} Paint", "Sunday {first}", "{first} Daylight"],
      "lines": [
        "I painted that sun on the back wall. Wrong colour. Nobody here remembers the right one.",
        "We grow beans under the lamps. They come up pale, but they come up.",
        "You keep the law, and then you find a little room inside it. That's where you live.",
        "Every Sunday we sweep the square like there'll be a fair. There's never a fair. It's clean, though.",
        "Fix one thing a day. A hinge. A sock. A face. That's how {town} keeps going.",
        "I keep a list of good things. It's short. I read it to {name} at night.",
        "Bring us something from out there. A stone, a leaf. The children have never held a leaf.",
        "We hold a fair for the first snow. No noise. Paper lanterns. You'd be surprised what we manage."
      ]
    },
    "restless": {
      "bynames": ["{first} Away", "{first} the Train", "{first} Mainland"],
      "lines": [
        "Where does the line go, past the last fort? Tell me true. I'll not tell anyone.",
        "I've a bag packed under the bed. It's been packed since the walls went up.",
        "Take me with you. ... I'm joking. Unless you'd say yes.",
        "{other}. Have you been? What's it like? Is it like here?",
        "They say the walls keep us safe. They keep us something.",
        "One day I'll walk out that gate and keep walking till I see the sea. The real one, not the painted one.",
        "I watch the trains go. Not come. Go.",
        "Do you ever get used to it out there? I'd get used to it. I know I would."
      ]
    }
  }
}
